findings.body:
**Stop the reuse check from blocking fresh dispatch when the retained log is missing or unreadable.**

When a reusable cycle is selected, a missing or unreadable retained log throws inside the host-lock callback. The catch then returns `needs-human`, so the review never dispatches. The ledger gets no reuse record, so the same selection is found on the next call. Every `dev.review` at that identity stays blocked until the tree changes. If the retained log is deleted or unreadable, the author has no path to a new review.

Return `null`-style "no reuse" for these cases. Dispatch then proceeds as it does when no cycle is selected:

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
         if (selection === null) return;
-        if (effects.reviewLogSha256 === undefined) {
-          throw new Error('retained review log validation is unavailable');
-        }
-        const retainedDigest = await effects.reviewLogSha256(selection.cycle.logPath);
+        if (effects.reviewLogSha256 === undefined) return; // cannot validate: no reuse
+        let retainedDigest: string;
+        try {
+          retainedDigest = await effects.reviewLogSha256(selection.cycle.logPath);
+        } catch {
+          return; // retained log unreadable: no reuse, dispatch fresh
+        }
         if (
           selection.cycle.logSha256 !== undefined &&
           retainedDigest !== selection.cycle.logSha256
         ) {
           throw new Error('retained review log digest does not match');
         }
```

</details>

A recorded digest that does not match still stops the review. The inspected code does not show whether that hard stop is intended as tamper detection. Keep it unless the ledger contract says otherwise.
